          "date": "2026-09-06 22:04:59.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20348 tests: count only client-side ldlm namespaces",
        "message": "LU-20348 tests: count only client-side ldlm namespaces\n\nremount_client_normally() verifies that no ldlm namespace is left\nover once the client has been remounted, but ldlm.namespaces.* also\nmatches the server-side namespaces. Where the client shares a node\nwith the servers the count can never reach MDSCOUNT+OSTCOUNT+1, so\nevery encryption subtest fails in cleanup. Count only the client\nside namespaces, and log the whole list when the count is wrong.\n\nFixes: 7d75520980a0 (\"LU-19449 tests: survive sysfs leftovers in test cleanup\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: Icc4150c33bb8dcfd29bd99a8a0502eb7314bc9ad\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68254\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Sebastien Buisson <sbuisson@ddn.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
